(- Cookie format \(decoded\): user|role|sha1\(SECRET || "user|role"\)) Tj
T*
(- Protected page: GET /admin returns the flag if admin is present in the parsed fields.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Solution) Tj
T*
(The server signs SHA1\(SECRET || message\). Because SHA-1 is Merkle-Damgard, knowing the hash of) Tj
T*
(an unknown-prefix message allows computing the hash of:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECRET || message || glue_padding || extra) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(without knowing SECRET.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Steps) Tj
T*
(1. Fetch a valid cookie via GET /profile.) Tj
T*
(2. Base64-decode to split message and sig.) Tj
T*
(3. Perform SHA-1 length extension to append |admin to the message.) Tj
T*
(4. Re-encode the forged cookie and request GET /admin with it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Reproduction) Tj
T*
(1. Run the challenge \(Python + Flask\): python challenges/web-cookie-smith/app.py \(listens on) Tj
T*
(http://localhost:5001\).) Tj
T*
(2. Run the exploit: python exploits/exploit_cookie_smith.py.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Flag) Tj
T*
(flag{length_extension_broke_auth}) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Mitigation) Tj
T*
(- Replace secret-prefix hashing with an HMAC: HMAC-SHA256\(secret, message\).) Tj
T*
(- Do not store authorization decisions \(like role\) in client-controlled data unless it is) Tj
T*
(strongly authenticated and validated.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
