(# Web: SQLi in Search) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Summary) Tj
T*
(Exploit a UNION-based SQL injection in a SQLite-backed search endpoint to read the flags table.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Challenge) Tj
T*
(- Endpoint: GET /search?q=<input>) Tj
T*
(- Vulnerable query shape:) Tj
T*
(      SELECT title FROM posts WHERE title LIKE '%<q>%') Tj
T*
(- App also echoes SQLite exceptions to the client \(useful for discovery\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Solution) Tj
T*
(Because q is interpolated into SQL without parameters, we can terminate the string and append a) Tj
T*
(UNION SELECT that returns the flag.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Steps) Tj
T*
(1. Confirm injection: q=' OR 1=1 -- should return all posts.) Tj
T*
(2. Because the original query selects 1 column \(title\), use a 1-column UNION payload.) Tj
T*
(3. Extract flag: q=' UNION SELECT flag FROM flags --) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
